= Evaluation

/*
Present your evaluation methodology and results by addressing the following:
• What hypotheses did you test?
• What testing procedures did you conduct to validate your system?
• Describe your experimental procedure: what tasks did participants perform?
• Identify your independent, dependent, and control variables.
• Did you use a within-subjects, between-subjects, or mixed experimental design?
• Report your results and indicate whether they achieve statistical significance.
Your experiment should measure:
1. Behavioral response: Measure user performance on tasks across various conditions according to your hypotheses. 
2. Subjective response: Capture user impressions and sensations through questionnaires administered at the end of the experiment and/or between experimental conditions.
Consider reporting your pilot study results, particularly if they helped you refine your system or experimental procedure.
